# Life data — never in git
data/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.pytest*/
.ruff_cache/
.uv-cache/
*.cloud-sync.json
*.cloud-sync.lock
*.cloud-access.json
*.cloud-access.lock
*.cloud-access.json.*.tmp
*.cloud-archive.json
*.cloud-computer.json
*.cloud-computer.json.tmp
*.cloud-archive.lock
varyz-cloud.sqlite3*
dist/
.build-cache/

# Local previews, private document work and plugin repair snapshots are not release inputs.
/output/
/tmp/
/.plugin-*.py

# Local config with machine-specific paths (config.example.toml IS tracked)
config.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Model caches
.fastembed_cache/

# Raw eval output — lists absolute paths of every indexed file. Regenerable:
# scripts/evaluate_retrieval.py --json-out
reports/baseline_*.json

# Private, resumable agent A/B transcripts and gold evidence. Dated aggregate
# reports may be committed; raw model context must not be.
reports/agent_ab_runs/

# 2026-08-30: and a run's own JSON is raw model context. The A/B campaign of
# 2026-08-23 wrote 106 of these; 47 of them quote the archive verbatim in
# `source_message`, `quotes`, `proposition` and `exact_literal` fields, and the
# QWEN_REVIEW dumps name the chats and the people who wrote the messages. None
# of that belongs in a public repository, and none of it is the finding: the
# finding is in the report written beside it. So the written .md reports are
# committed and the machine-written evidence stays here. If a particular JSON
# really should be public, read it first and `git add -f` it deliberately.
# Already-tracked report JSON is unaffected by this line and was checked
# separately.
reports/*.json
reports/*.txt

# A compile's own console log, written next to the reports it belongs with. It
# is the raw transcript -- entry ids, window text, the names of the people the
# annotator was reading -- and the finding is in the dated report beside it.
reports/*.log

# Business documents -- pricing, strategy, creator terms. They are written next to
# the docs they reference but are not part of the AGPL source, and the repository
# is going public.
docs/private/

# Dated run reports and the old site comparisons stay on the owner's machine
# (decided 2026-09-25). Code comments may still name a report; it is the local
# record of a measurement, not something a user needs.
reports/
website-comparison/
# Operational measurements remain private even when an earlier run wrote them in docs.
/docs/*_CAPACITY_20??-??-??.*
/docs/CLOUD_SPIKE_PROTECTION_20??-??-??.*

# Where a session parks a one-off script it needed for a single operation. It is
# working material for one machine on one day, not part of the tool.
.scratch/

# Safety snapshots made by the unattended compile supervisor must live outside
# `data/`: `varyz backup` deliberately refuses to copy an archive into itself.
.compile-backups/

# What a script wrote while it ran, next to the script. `purge_scratch_dirs.ps1`
# logs the repository root it worked in, which is the owner's home directory --
# the mark the publication audit exists to catch. The script is the artefact
# worth keeping; its log is one run of it on one machine.
scripts/*.log

# Scratch archives written by tests that need a real data directory. They are
# throwaway, and 78 of them once made `git status` unreadable in this repo.
.test-tmp-*/
.test-tmp/
.tmp_public_eval_tests_*/
# The egress failure-path tests deliberately make their archive unreadable, so
# git cannot even stat what is inside them.
.pytest-tmp-*/
.pytest-tmp/
.tmp/
.tmp-*
/.deploy-secrets/

# One directory in this repository is a bug's fossil, not a scratch archive: a
# 2026-08-13 session wrote a Windows temp path through a shell that ate the
# backslashes, so an absolute path landed here as one relative name. It is
# unreadable without elevation, which is why it is still here, and it makes
# `git status` warn on every run until it is ignored. Delete it in the same
# elevated shell that clears the .test-tmp-* directories.
Usersegor*/

# The public tree is the code, its tests and fixtures, and the docs a user reads
# (decided 2026-09-27). Plans, work queues, launch notes and the site the alpha
# does not ship stay on the owner's machine. Code comments may still name one of
# these; like a report, it is the local record the comment was written against.
.claude/
pivot/
TODO.md
MANIFEST.md
docs/BUILD.md
docs/PIVOT_PLAN.md
docs/TEMPORAL_TRUTH_AND_PRIVATE_CONTEXT.md
docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md
docs/SHIPPING.md
website/
scripts/site/

# Local build logs and Cloud sync state
.build-cache-*.log
config.cloud-reports.json
config.cloud-reports.lock
